Subject: Cache shapes for static object literals

Technical overview
  Records eligible object-literal sites during compilation and stores their
  static atom keys in the function bytecode. A dedicated opcode dispatches
  templated literals in O(1) time; the first execution builds a normal hashed
  shape for the current realm and later executions allocate directly from it.

  Template metadata is serialized with bytecode so compiled bundles retain the
  optimization. Cached shapes remain runtime-only and are rebuilt after loading;
  unsupported literals keep the existing generic path.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The new opcode and serialized template metadata change the bytecode
  format, so older bytecode must be rejected.


